n be found via get_user_details. They might need to choose one, or the default can be used.\n\nAlso, the user is impatient, so I should be efficient. Let me outline the steps: authenticate user, get user details, find the correct order and item, find the new item, confirm payment method, then execute the exchange. Each step requires a tool call. Let's start with authentication.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"find_user_id_by_name_zip\", \"arguments\": {\"first_name\": \"Lei\", \"last_name\": \"Wilson\", \"zip\": \"32255\"}}\n",
